            "target_entity_instance": "CH4 emissions",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "ORCHIDEE provides CH4 emissions by natural wetlands as the product of a flux density by a wetland extent, at a 1\u00b0 resolution for the time period 1990\u20132009.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "El-Ni\u00f1o",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Tropics",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The 1997-99 large growth rate anomaly is explained by a positive anomaly in emissions from biomass burning, both in the Tropics and at high latitudes (van der Werf et al., 2006; Langenfelds et al., 2002), together with a negative anomaly in emissions from tropical wetlands in 97\u201398, linked to dry El-Ni\u00f1o conditions, followed by a positive anomaly in the same emissions in 98\u201399, linked to wet La-Ni\u00f1a conditions (Bousquet et al., 2006; Chen and Prinn, 2006).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "La-Ni\u00f1a",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Tropics",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The 1997-99 large growth rate anomaly is explained by a positive anomaly in emissions from biomass burning, both in the Tropics and at high latitudes (van der Werf et al., 2006; Langenfelds et al., 2002), together with a negative anomaly in emissions from tropical wetlands in 97\u201398, linked to dry El-Ni\u00f1o conditions, followed by a positive anomaly in the same emissions in 98\u201399, linked to wet La-Ni\u00f1a conditions (Bousquet et al., 2006; Chen and Prinn, 2006).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
